# Direct IPs and CIDRs added verbatim to the ipset (no DNS lookup).
# Use this for CDN-fronted hosts whose edge pool rotates IPs across a /24
# (Azure Front Door, Fastly, Akamai, Edgio, Google global LB, ...).
# Symptom of needing an entry here: ~135-second curl timeouts despite the
# hostname being in allowed-domains.list. See README for the full playbook.
# One entry per line. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.

# Project DB server (reachable via Windows-host VPN)
172.23.7.5
172.23.7.6

# Fastly edge /24s fronting deb.debian.org (and the debian.map.fastly.net pool).
# 2026-08-31: boot-time resolve pinned ...2/66/130/194.217 but the client was being
# steered to ...2/66/130/194.132 — same four /24s, rotated last octet — so apt failed
# with an instant REJECT on IPv4 and then printed misleading "Network is unreachable"
# IPv6 errors. Pin the /24s so last-octet rotation inside the pool cannot break apt.
151.101.2.0/24
151.101.66.0/24
151.101.130.0/24
151.101.194.0/24

# Local LAN Windows box on the home Wi-Fi (192.168.1.0/24). Reached via WSL2 NAT
# through the Windows host, which is on the same LAN. Single host only -- do NOT
# widen to the /24: that would open the whole home network to the isolated distro.
192.168.1.102

# Microsoft 365 — deliberately NARROW. Microsoft publishes five SharePoint
# ranges (13.107.136.0/22, 40.108.128.0/17, 52.104.0.0/14, 104.146.128.0/17,
# 150.171.40.0/22 = ~330k addresses serving *every* tenant worldwide, i.e. a
# ready-made exfil path). Only the smallest is pinned; the CGI tenant front-end
# resolves inside it. Widen only if Excel-for-the-web actually breaks.
13.107.136.0/22          # SharePoint Online front-end (M365 endpoint id=31)
# Entra ID auth endpoints (id=56) — identity only, no file storage.
20.190.128.0/18
40.126.0.0/18
20.20.32.0/19

# Azure Front Door edge pool that fronts code.visualstudio.com (rotates IPs in /24)
150.171.110.0/24

# Fastly edge pool that fronts vscode.download.prss.microsoft.com (VS Code Server + CLI binaries)
146.75.106.0/24

# Google global LB range fronting downloads.claude.ai (rotates)
35.190.0.0/16

# Akamai edge /24 fronting playwright.download.prss.microsoft.com (Edge browser binaries).
# The host straddles Fastly (146.75.106.0/24 above) and Akamai; this covers the Akamai half.
23.219.160.0/24

# Edgio/Limelight edge /24s fronting docs.stripe.com. Last octet rotates so
# dig-at-boot misses the IP the client is steered to; pin the whole /24.
198.137.150.0/24
198.202.176.0/24

# Cloudflare edge /24s fronting cdn.sheetjs.com (xlsx tarball pulled by npm install).
# Cloudflare anycast — pinning the two A-records would break on edge rotation.
104.21.80.0/24
172.67.172.0/24

# Cloudflare edge /24s fronting releases.openai.com (Codex CLI installer binaries,
# pulled by https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.sh). Anycast — pin the /24s, not the A-records.
172.64.144.0/24
104.18.43.0/24

# Cloudflare edge /24s fronting fireworks.ai (site/docs). Anycast — the two
# A-records resolved at reload time rotate; pin the /24s. Note api.fireworks.ai
# is GCP-hosted (35.207.x) and already covered by the goog.json live fetch.
104.18.6.0/24
104.18.7.0/24

# Vercel edge /24s fronting app.fireworks.ai (Fireworks web console, CNAME into
# *.vercel-dns-013.com). Two A-records that rotate; pin the /24s. Also covers
# vercel.com, which currently lands in the same 64.239.109.0/24 pool.
64.239.109.0/24
64.239.123.0/24

# Cloudflare edge /24s fronting pi.dev / www.pi.dev. Anycast — pin the /24s.
104.21.62.0/24
172.67.221.0/24

# Yahoo IMAP (imap.mail.yahoo.com → jimapinternal.imap.mail.g03.yahoodns.net).
# The pool is larger than what any single resolve returns and varies BY RESOLVER,
# so pin the /24s rather than the A-records. Reached on 993/tcp — the OUTPUT allow
# rule is destination-IP only and does not filter by port, so no extra port rule.
#
# 2026-08-31: Yahoo ADDED two /24s. The distro resolver and 1.1.1.1/9.9.9.9 now
# return only the 98.x pair, while 8.8.8.8 still returns all four:
#   8.8.8.8 -> 98.136.96.39  98.137.156.39  67.195.176.151  69.147.112.172
#   1.1.1.1 -> 98.137.156.39 98.136.96.39
# The 67./69. pins matched nothing the client was being steered to, which broke
# IMAP poll while SMTP kept working (its 66.163.170.0/24 pin was still current).
# Keep all four: the older two are still live in the pool, just not handed out here.
67.195.176.0/24
69.147.112.0/24
98.137.156.0/24
98.136.96.0/24

# Yahoo SMTP (smtp.mail.yahoo.com → smtp.mail.global.gm0.yahoodns.net).
# Pool spans two /24s and varies by resolver (2026-08-11: 8.8.8.8 → 66.218.88.167
# + 66.163.170.52; 1.1.1.1 and 9.9.9.9 → 66.163.170.52 only). A bare hostname
# pins whichever single A record boot happened to get, so send works some boots
# and hangs on others — pin both /24s, same as Yahoo IMAP above. Reached on
# 465/587 tcp; the OUTPUT allow rule is destination-IP only, no port rule needed.
66.218.88.0/24
66.163.170.0/24

# Cloudflare edge /24s fronting hub.ag3nts.org (AI agents course platform).
104.21.63.0/24
172.67.170.0/24

